# Local use only: `npm run dev` reads .env and .env.local; `npm run check` and the MCP server (mcp/server.js)
# read .env.local. In production the key is a Worker secret (`npx wrangler secret put TYPESAFE_API_KEY`)
# and the settings live in wrangler.jsonc.
# One key is enough. With both set TypeSafe is used; JEV_PROVIDER=openrouter switches over.
# TypeSafe's own API: https://typesafe.ai
TYPESAFE_API_KEY=
# OpenRouter's Decisions API: https://openrouter.ai/settings/keys
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# JEVTOWN_MCP_DAILY_BUDGET_USD=1   # dollars one MCP server may spend per UTC day, and every client starts its own; 0 = no limit
# JEVTOWN_MCP_MAX_SECONDS=45       # a check starts the next wave only if it expects to finish within this, follow-up included; 0 = no limit
